WEBVTT

00:01.710 --> 00:06.670
<b>KAEI YEAR 6 (1853)</b>

00:04.460 --> 00:06.670
<b>SUGAYA</b>

00:11.170 --> 00:14.040
<b>Feel free to take a drink and wet your whistle.</b>

00:15.460 --> 00:16.380
<b>All right.</b>

00:32.170 --> 00:36.670
<b>Now then, I'll get straight to the point.
I have a job for you.</b>

00:37.460 --> 00:42.000
<b>The owner of a fine arts store in Tenmacho
came to me with some concerns</b>

00:42.170 --> 00:44.040
<b>about a peculiar piece that he procured recently.</b>

00:45.880 --> 00:48.040
<b>A demonic painting, apparently.</b>

00:49.130 --> 00:53.630
<b>It's known by the name: "The Ukiyo-e of Kudanzaka."</b>

00:54.380 --> 00:57.710
<b>With a reputation like that,
I'm guessing there are strange rumors attached to it?</b>

00:58.210 --> 01:00.580
<b>Well, more than just rumors.</b>

01:01.250 --> 01:06.170
<b>From my understanding, the artist who painted it
has become bedridden with an illness.</b>

01:06.880 --> 01:10.920
<b>And he claims it's the demons getting
their vengeance on him for selling this painting.</b>

01:12.000 --> 01:12.960
<b>What do you think?</b>

01:14.920 --> 01:17.630
<b>It seems like a regular paining, as far as I can tell.</b>

01:17.880 --> 01:23.080
<b>However, real paranormal objects
only show their true colors under the right conditions.</b>

01:23.630 --> 01:25.250
<b>Yes, of course.</b>

01:25.880 --> 01:27.830
<b>If we're lucky, it's harmless.</b>

01:27.920 --> 01:32.580
<b>But if it turns out that it could bring trouble,
then I want you to take care of it.</b>

01:33.830 --> 01:35.170
<b>Consider it done.</b>

01:35.630 --> 01:39.040
<b>Of course, I don't expect you to do it for free.</b>

01:39.330 --> 01:41.170
<b>I'll make sure you're fairly paid.</b>

01:41.880 --> 01:43.080
<b>I appreciate that.</b>

01:44.960 --> 01:48.920
<b>Once this is settled,
why don't we share a good drink or two?</b>

03:26.670 --> 03:29.460
<b>Why hello, Jinya-kun. Welcome in!</b>

03:29.460 --> 03:30.420
<b>Take a seat.</b>

03:32.000 --> 03:33.630
<b>You must've been cold out there.</b>

03:35.500 --> 03:36.880
<b>Want some kake-soba?</b>

03:36.880 --> 03:37.580
<b>Yes.</b>

03:38.880 --> 03:40.040
<b>Is Jinya here?!</b>

03:40.920 --> 03:42.040
<b>Oh, thank goodness.</b>

03:42.670 --> 03:46.460
<b>Please, I need your help!
There's this Ukiyo-e of Kudanzaka, ya see...</b>

03:47.040 --> 03:48.830
<b>The Ukiyo-e of Kudanzaka?</b>

03:49.170 --> 03:52.000
<b>That's right. It's some kinda demonic painting.</b>

03:52.330 --> 03:55.790
<b>Everybody's saying that it's cursed because the guy
who owned it died in a bizarre way.</b>

03:56.580 --> 03:58.210
<b>Looks like it's been ripped.</b>

03:58.580 --> 04:01.000
<b>Yeah. Cuz I accidentally dropped it.</b>

04:01.130 --> 04:03.630
<b>A bewitched painting that got ripped?!</b>

04:03.630 --> 04:06.420
<b>You're gonna jinx my shop by bringing that in here!</b>

04:06.420 --> 04:08.000
<b>Oh, I'm sorry, sir.</b>

04:09.830 --> 04:10.790
<b>Take a look at this.</b>

04:11.500 --> 04:13.710
<b>Whoa. What the hell?</b>

04:13.710 --> 04:16.210
<b>The owner of a fine arts store in Tenmacho
acquired this painting,</b>

04:16.460 --> 04:19.040
<b>it's apparently known as the Ukiyo-e of Kudanzaka.</b>

04:19.500 --> 04:21.750
<b>This was also described to me as a "demonic painting."</b>

04:22.170 --> 04:24.830
<b>It looks exactly like the one that I brought.</b>

04:25.630 --> 04:30.040
<b>Let me get this straight. There are multiple copies
of a supposedly "bewitched" painting on the market?</b>

04:30.040 --> 04:32.000
<b>Something doesn't add up here.</b>

04:32.290 --> 04:33.330
<b>Indeed.</b>

04:34.040 --> 04:36.290
<b>It's quite a beautiful painting.</b>

04:36.830 --> 04:39.670
<b>Can you gleam anything from it, Zenji-san?</b>

04:39.830 --> 04:41.080
<b>Well, let's see...</b>

04:41.380 --> 04:45.130
<b>The color has hardly faded and the paper
doesn't show any deterioration.</b>

04:45.420 --> 04:48.040
<b>So I doubt even a year has passed since it was made.</b>

04:48.500 --> 04:52.080
<b>You know, I'm familiar with the folks
who run that fine arts shop in Tenmacho.</b>

04:52.380 --> 04:55.670
<b>If I call in a favor, they'll trace it back
to the artist for me.</b>

04:55.920 --> 04:57.170
<b>I would appreciate that.</b>

04:57.460 --> 05:00.920
<b>No biggie! I already owe you
for helping Lady Natsu all the time.</b>

05:01.170 --> 05:03.830
<b>This is the least I can do to return the favor!</b>

05:07.290 --> 05:09.330
<b>Just wait here. I'll go ask.</b>

05:13.000 --> 05:14.670
<b>Ah, if it isn't Zenji-san!</b>

05:15.210 --> 05:18.000
<b>Good timing. We got a new stock of smut in.</b>

05:18.000 --> 05:20.250
<b>Sorry! I'll have to save that for next time!</b>

05:21.210 --> 05:24.880
<b>Say, pops, do you have the Ukiyo-e of Kudanzaka here?</b>

05:25.130 --> 05:28.210
<b>No, I actually took that piece down.</b>

05:28.880 --> 05:33.290
<b>People are saying it's demonic,
so I didn't feel good about displaying it inside the store.</b>

05:33.830 --> 05:36.290
<b>Isn't that just some baloney the artist made up?</b>

05:36.540 --> 05:37.210
<b>No.</b>

05:37.920 --> 05:40.920
<b>I know for a fact the artist is bedridden from illness.</b>

05:41.880 --> 05:46.000
<b>And worse yet, word on the street is that
someone who bought the painting got killed.</b>

05:47.000 --> 05:49.790
<b>I don't want any ugly rumors
being associated with my shop.</b>

05:50.000 --> 05:52.290
<b>Well, that's understandable.</b>

05:53.080 --> 05:56.330
<b>By the way, does that painter
live anywhere around here?</b>

06:00.000 --> 06:01.080
<b>Thanks for waiting!</b>

06:01.920 --> 06:03.080
<b>What do you have there?</b>

06:03.420 --> 06:05.170
<b>Ah, j-just a little something!</b>

06:05.920 --> 06:07.670
<b>More importantly, I got the details.</b>

06:08.080 --> 06:10.580
<b>They told me the painter lives in Sakaicho.</b>

06:10.960 --> 06:13.830
<b>Thank you. I'll handle the rest myself.</b>

06:14.580 --> 06:15.790
<b>Be careful!</b>

06:16.250 --> 06:16.750
<b>Right.</b>

06:23.670 --> 06:26.710
<b>Pardon! Is Doshu Saga-dono available?</b>

06:27.290 --> 06:29.790
<b>Yeah! Come on in.</b>

06:33.830 --> 06:36.420
<b>Been a long time since I've had any visitors.</b>

06:37.290 --> 06:38.540
<b>Who might you be?</b>

06:38.960 --> 06:41.380
<b>Greetings. I am known as Jinya.</b>

06:41.630 --> 06:44.630
<b>I have made my way here
to seek your knowledge, good sir.</b>

06:45.210 --> 06:49.170
<b>You can drop the formalities.
I ain't important enough for 'em.</b>

06:49.710 --> 06:51.040
<b>Have a seat.</b>

07:03.790 --> 07:07.080
<b>I was told that you had fallen quite ill, Saga-dono.</b>

07:07.170 --> 07:12.750
<b>Nothing as serious as that.
Just old age catching up with me.</b>

07:13.330 --> 07:17.210
<b>My body can't handle the strain of making art anymore.</b>

07:18.330 --> 07:20.380
<b>So, it's not the curse of a demonic painting?</b>

07:20.580 --> 07:25.670
<b>Hah. What gave you that idea, sourpuss?
You work at Sengendo or something?</b>

07:26.080 --> 07:27.250
<b>Not at all.</b>

07:27.830 --> 07:29.960
<b>But I did hear that you were the one who painted this.</b>

07:31.330 --> 07:32.580
<b>Kudanzaka...</b>

07:33.080 --> 07:35.540
<b>Now that takes me back!</b>

07:36.250 --> 07:40.290
<b>I've been investigating the rumors behind
the Ukiyo-e of Kudanzaka to find out if they're true.</b>

07:40.630 --> 07:43.330
<b>Would you please tell me what you know about it?</b>

07:44.210 --> 07:46.460
<b>Sure, I can do that.</b>

07:47.210 --> 07:49.130
<b>But where to start?</b>

07:50.040 --> 07:55.630
<b>Firstly, the name "Kudanzaka."
It has no relation to the Kudanzaka locale in Edo.</b>

07:55.790 --> 07:57.580
<b>It actually refers to the woman.</b>

07:58.670 --> 08:01.750
<b>Do you mean to say it's the name
of this lady in the picture?</b>

08:02.250 --> 08:04.040
<b>Not quite.</b>

08:04.380 --> 08:08.830
<b>Way back when, a fella who carried a katana
forged in Kadono came up with that moniker.</b>

08:10.960 --> 08:12.630
<b>Kudanzaka or "nine hills."</b>

08:13.130 --> 08:17.080
<b>His name was Motoharu and he used to visit here often.</b>

08:26.920 --> 08:29.130
<b>Couldn't even protect the woman I love.</b>

08:29.580 --> 08:32.710
<b>Dammit. It doesn't get more pathetic than that.</b>

08:34.500 --> 08:36.210
<b>Hey, Jinta.</b>

08:38.330 --> 08:42.080
<b>To be honest, I actually hated Yokaze when we first met.</b>

08:43.170 --> 08:47.960
<b>I felt lucky to become a sentinel, but she drove me nuts
because I couldn't make sense of her.</b>

08:49.460 --> 08:53.000
<b>Still, that hatred didn't stop me
from wanting to keep her safe.</b>

08:54.540 --> 08:56.170
<b>But now look at us...</b>

08:57.250 --> 09:00.210
<b>Everything in life changes with the passage of time.</b>

09:01.420 --> 09:05.210
<b>Even my indelible oath to protect her
couldn't last forever.</b>

09:06.630 --> 09:08.540
<b>Don't end up like me, all right?</b>

09:09.710 --> 09:13.960
<b>Jinta. Become a man who can cherish his hatred.</b>

09:19.580 --> 09:20.500
<b>You're in charge now!</b>

09:21.000 --> 09:24.420
<b>Take care of Shirayuki. And stay close with Suzune.</b>

09:25.170 --> 09:25.710
<b>Okay?</b>

09:32.790 --> 09:34.830
<b>I'm sorry, but that man...</b>

09:35.500 --> 09:38.170
<b>Could you please tell me a little more about him?</b>

09:38.830 --> 09:39.460
<b>Hm?</b>

09:40.000 --> 09:43.880
<b>I hail from Kadono. Motoharu was my foster father.</b>

09:44.330 --> 09:48.960
<b>Oh, you don't say? So, you're his foster son!</b>

09:49.580 --> 09:51.290
<b>I'll gladly tell you more.</b>

09:51.540 --> 09:56.290
<b>I can't really explain about Kudanzaka without
going into more detail about Motoharu, anyways.</b>

09:58.500 --> 10:00.750
<b>Back when I was still a young whippersnapper...</b>

10:09.500 --> 10:11.960
<b>Hey, lady. Do you live here?</b>

10:13.290 --> 10:14.880
<b>Yes, I do.</b>

10:15.630 --> 10:18.170
<b>Well, I'm moving in today. The name's Doshu Saga.</b>

10:18.630 --> 10:19.290
<b>And you are?</b>

10:20.580 --> 10:23.130
<b>I cannot share my name, but I never lie.</b>

10:23.330 --> 10:25.250
<b>You may just call me "Nameless."</b>

10:25.920 --> 10:27.000
<b>Nameless...?</b>

10:35.080 --> 10:37.380
<b>Wow. You're really buckling down today.</b>

10:37.830 --> 10:39.170
<b>Finishing another masterpiece?</b>

10:39.630 --> 10:43.130
<b>You bet! I'm gonna be the best artist in Edo, ya know.</b>

10:43.750 --> 10:45.130
<b>Now that's rich.</b>

10:45.130 --> 10:47.250
<b>It's no joke. I'm serious!</b>

10:48.460 --> 10:49.170
<b>If you say so.</b>

10:52.170 --> 10:54.210
<b>I'm Motoharu, the sentinel.</b>

10:54.540 --> 10:58.040
<b>I have come under orders
from the Itsukihime to deliver a letter.</b>

10:58.420 --> 11:00.420
<b>Oh, it's just you again.</b>

11:01.000 --> 11:02.000
<b>Dammit.</b>

11:02.750 --> 11:05.960
<b>Why am I running around like a messenger
when I'm supposed to be a sentinel?!</b>

11:06.540 --> 11:07.790
<b>It's bullshit!</b>

11:08.330 --> 11:10.170
<b>That woman is seriously obnoxious!</b>

11:12.710 --> 11:17.630
<b>More bitching? You never have anything good to say
about this Itsukihime lady.</b>

11:18.170 --> 11:19.290
<b>Well, yeah, obviously!</b>

11:19.540 --> 11:23.920
<b>I thought I'd finally earned some respect with this job,
but I just get sent off to Edo like a servant.</b>

11:24.670 --> 11:27.540
<b>I swear, that woman is more demonic
than actual demons!</b>

11:32.670 --> 11:38.790
<b>Your father was a hoot. He'd come down to Edo
once a year just to blow off steam with his complaining.</b>

11:39.080 --> 11:40.630
<b>Did he really?</b>

11:40.880 --> 11:45.380
<b>Let me guess. He always watched his mouth
and acted like a proper gentleman around you?</b>

11:46.630 --> 11:49.880
<b>Sorry to say, but he was actually pretty hotheaded.</b>

11:51.210 --> 11:54.670
<b>Anyways, back to the topic of Kudanzaka...</b>

11:55.330 --> 12:00.960
<b>It was originally a beni-e that I painted
by hand when Nameless still lived around here.</b>

12:01.420 --> 12:04.750
<b>But much later, the folks from Sengendo told me
they were interested in selling it.</b>

12:05.420 --> 12:10.750
<b>The pieces on the market now are woodblock prints
carved from a new sketch of it that I made for them.</b>

12:11.750 --> 12:15.080
<b>So, then, it's a painting of the woman
you knew as Nameless?</b>

12:15.830 --> 12:19.170
<b>You could say that, but it's not entirely accurate.</b>

12:20.170 --> 12:24.380
<b>You've described Kudanzaka
to people as a "demonic painting." Why is that?</b>

12:25.080 --> 12:27.920
<b>Believe it or not, that's exactly what it is.</b>

12:28.460 --> 12:31.330
<b>At its core, that painting has been "bewitched" for sure.</b>

12:32.790 --> 12:38.210
<b>However, before we get into the nitty-gritty,
there's something I have to ask you first.</b>

12:39.080 --> 12:42.040
<b>What did you think when you saw
Kudanzaka for the first time?</b>

12:46.080 --> 12:49.710
<b>Seeing the Miko wearing a jade necklace
next to a river made me think</b>

12:49.710 --> 12:53.250
<b>of the legend of Princess Nunakawa from Shinano.</b>

12:54.250 --> 12:56.080
<b>Except the katana that she's holding</b>

12:56.080 --> 12:59.750
<b>also gave me the impression it may be connected
to Kadono and the Itsukihime.</b>

13:00.210 --> 13:03.130
<b>Ah, very good. You're spot on.</b>

13:03.580 --> 13:06.000
<b>Then let me explain why its demonic.</b>

13:06.630 --> 13:09.580
<b>But just so you know,
I'm betting that you'll regret hearing this.</b>

13:10.170 --> 13:13.750
<b>You may end up feeling you were better off not knowing.</b>

13:19.580 --> 13:23.960
<b>Over the course of many years,
Motoharu would travel to Edo as part of his duties,</b>

13:24.380 --> 13:27.580
<b>and stop by here to complain
for a little while before going back.</b>

13:28.290 --> 13:32.830
<b>However, I noticed that his attitude
towards the Miko that he served began to change.</b>

13:33.500 --> 13:34.960
<b>Until, one day...</b>

13:36.960 --> 13:38.460
<b>I want you to paint something for me.</b>

13:39.080 --> 13:39.880
<b>Oh yeah?</b>

13:40.330 --> 13:42.460
<b>Let me guess, your beloved Miko?</b>

13:43.000 --> 13:44.000
<b>That's right.</b>

13:44.210 --> 13:47.040
<b>I remember the days
when all you did was bitch about her.</b>

13:47.040 --> 13:50.210
<b>Now you've skipped right to being
head over damn heels in love!</b>

13:50.500 --> 13:51.630
<b>Don't make fun of me.</b>

13:52.790 --> 13:56.420
<b>Besides... she's had her own struggles.</b>

13:57.500 --> 14:02.080
<b>All right, but how am I supposed
to paint a lady I ain't ever seen, huh?</b>

14:02.630 --> 14:04.000
<b>That won't be a problem.</b>

14:04.670 --> 14:06.420
<b>Because we have Nameless here.</b>

14:06.960 --> 14:09.670
<b>Nameless? What's she got to do with it?</b>

14:10.210 --> 14:11.460
<b>Well, you see...</b>

14:11.880 --> 14:14.330
<b>Nameless was originally born in Shinano,</b>

14:14.830 --> 14:18.040
<b>but it seems she faced some hardships
that forced her to flee to Kadono.</b>

14:18.750 --> 14:19.380
<b>Oh?</b>

14:19.670 --> 14:23.500
<b>Then she eventually left Kadono
and came to settle here in Edo.</b>

14:24.130 --> 14:29.250
<b>Hold on. I'll admit that comes as a surprise,
but what's it got to do with the painting of your Miko?</b>

14:29.250 --> 14:30.790
<b>Because those two are connected.</b>

14:31.330 --> 14:31.960
<b>Huh?</b>

14:32.830 --> 14:34.000
<b>The truth is that...</b>

14:35.000 --> 14:36.960
<b>Yokaze and Nameless are identical.</b>

14:37.880 --> 14:41.670
<b>You're telling me the Ukiyo-e of Kudanzaka
is a painting of Yokaze-san?</b>

14:42.670 --> 14:44.750
<b>The Miko of Kadono village?</b>

14:45.130 --> 14:46.920
<b>You got that right!</b>

14:47.670 --> 14:53.380
<b>It was painted based on her lookalike, Nameless,
combined with Motoharu's advice and my imagination.</b>

14:53.500 --> 14:55.130
<b>That's how Kudanzaka was born.</b>

14:56.750 --> 15:02.670
<b>Although it evokes the legend of Princess Nunakawa,
it actually depicts the Itsukihime and Yarai, huh?</b>

15:04.830 --> 15:06.500
<b>But what makes it demonic?</b>

15:07.170 --> 15:12.880
<b>Back in the early days, Motoharu once described that
woman as being "more demonic than actual demons."</b>

15:13.130 --> 15:14.540
<b>And that's where it comes from.</b>

15:15.000 --> 15:18.210
<b>I just called it that to poke fun at his old bitching.</b>

15:19.380 --> 15:25.080
<b>But after I made that new sketch of it at Sengendo
for nostalgia's sake, I really started feeling my old age.</b>

15:25.630 --> 15:27.920
<b>Even now, I think it was a mistake.</b>

15:28.460 --> 15:33.920
<b>That "demonic" painting was based on real human love
and now karma is punishing me for making money off it.</b>

15:34.580 --> 15:40.040
<b>So, the staff of Sengendo took your words at face value
and believed the bewitched painting caused you to fall ill.</b>

15:40.540 --> 15:44.960
<b>Yeah, that's really all it boils down to.
Just a poorly timed coincidence.</b>

15:45.540 --> 15:49.460
<b>There's nothing spooky or cursed about it.
It's a perfectly respectable painting.</b>

15:50.790 --> 15:53.380
<b>Why did you think I would regret learning this?</b>

15:53.790 --> 15:56.580
<b>That painting of Kudanzaka. She's a real beaut, eh?</b>

15:59.670 --> 16:01.580
<b>Okay! Whaddya think of this, Motoharu?</b>

16:02.630 --> 16:04.540
<b>Nope. It's awful.</b>

16:10.130 --> 16:12.000
<b>Have you even been listening to me?</b>

16:12.250 --> 16:13.750
<b>That's not what Yokaze looks like.</b>

16:21.670 --> 16:25.210
<b>You're still not happy with it?
Jeez, what am I supposed to do?</b>

16:26.580 --> 16:28.040
<b>Make her even more beautiful.</b>

16:29.040 --> 16:34.210
<b>To sum it up, Kudanzaka is Motoharu's
heavily embellished version of his beloved Miko.</b>

16:35.580 --> 16:37.540
<b>Now, here's the real kicker.</b>

16:38.710 --> 16:43.330
<b>You said when you first saw Kudanzaka
that she made you think of Princess Nunakawa,</b>

16:43.330 --> 16:44.830
<b>but Motoharu had a different idea.</b>

16:46.290 --> 16:52.750
<b>YASAKATOME-NO-KAMI</b>

16:46.290 --> 16:49.880
<b>He thought she looked a lot like
the Goddess Yasakatome.</b>

16:50.670 --> 16:52.210
<b>Are you familiar with her?</b>

16:52.830 --> 16:56.420
<b>When I was younger, Motoharu-san did teach me
a little about local mythology.</b>

16:56.960 --> 16:59.380
<b>She's a goddess worshipped
at the Suwa shrine in Shinano, yes?</b>

16:59.710 --> 17:04.880
<b>Exactly. He probably made that connection
because Nameless was born in Shinano,</b>

17:05.380 --> 17:09.170
<b>but go figure his adoptive son would also
compare her to a Shinano goddess.</b>

17:15.460 --> 17:17.380
<b>You seem pretty damn happy.</b>

17:18.000 --> 17:20.500
<b>So, you wanna do the honors and give her a name?</b>

17:20.920 --> 17:21.750
<b>A name?</b>

17:22.630 --> 17:24.170
<b>Good question...</b>

17:25.330 --> 17:26.880
<b>Maybe Yasakatome?</b>

17:27.540 --> 17:28.130
<b>No.</b>

17:28.750 --> 17:31.130
<b>My wife's beauty surpasses even that of the gods.</b>

17:31.130 --> 17:35.460
<b>If Yasaka means "eight hills,"
then I need to bump it up another notch.</b>

17:35.460 --> 17:37.250
<b>So, her name will be...</b>

17:38.830 --> 17:40.040
<b>Kudanzaka!</b>

17:41.130 --> 17:44.250
<b>See? I bet you wish I never told you now!</b>

17:44.750 --> 17:49.960
<b>The Ukiyo-e of Kudanzaka is the result of your dad
being a lovesick puppy. He just wanted to glorify his wife.</b>

17:50.460 --> 17:54.420
<b>BEWITCHING:</b>

17:50.460 --> 17:54.420
<b>CURSED</b>

17:50.460 --> 17:54.420
<b>ATTRACTIVE</b>

17:50.460 --> 17:53.670
<b>And that's what makes it "bewitching."</b>

17:54.790 --> 18:00.500
<b>I get it now. His fawning led to Kudanzaka being
called "bewitching" for her beauty and not a curse.</b>

18:00.880 --> 18:05.420
<b>Speaking of, buddy, I notice you keep calling
her "Kudanzaka" without batting an eye,</b>

18:05.580 --> 18:10.080
<b>but I hope you realize that's basically like saying
"my mom's more beautiful than the gods."</b>

18:11.040 --> 18:12.790
<b>Oh, give me a break.</b>

18:15.130 --> 18:18.000
<b>You finally got that sourpuss look off your face!</b>

18:18.960 --> 18:20.580
<b>Thanks for the good laugh.</b>

18:21.170 --> 18:25.210
<b>Well, I suppose if you didn't
know about Kudanzaka until just now,</b>

18:25.540 --> 18:28.330
<b>that means Motoharu never shared her with his kids.</b>

18:31.290 --> 18:31.960
<b>Here.</b>

18:34.250 --> 18:35.130
<b>What's this?</b>

18:35.670 --> 18:37.710
<b>A test painting that I made back then.</b>

18:38.130 --> 18:41.130
<b>I hope you'll overlook the fact it's gotten a bit dirty.</b>

18:42.130 --> 18:46.460
<b>I know that I harped on him a lot,
but please don't hold a grudge against Motoharu.</b>

18:46.880 --> 18:50.420
<b>Despite being a dumbass, he truly cared for his family.</b>

18:51.040 --> 18:54.830
<b>He made fewer and fewer trips to Edo
after his daughter was born.</b>

18:54.830 --> 19:01.210
<b>Then, on his last visit, he told me about his new
adoptive son and daughter, and never came back.</b>

19:01.670 --> 19:03.170
<b>That's the kind of guy he was.</b>

19:12.580 --> 19:14.500
<b>Yeah, I know.</b>

19:15.710 --> 19:20.210
<b>My father was always teaching me important life lessons.</b>

19:22.380 --> 19:23.630
<b>That's good.</b>

19:27.880 --> 19:29.630
<b>Here's your order of kake-soba.</b>

19:31.210 --> 19:34.670
<b>What seems to be the problem, pal? You're staring at me.</b>

19:35.290 --> 19:38.330
<b>Nothing. Just admiring how good of a dad you are.</b>

19:38.710 --> 19:39.380
<b>Huh?</b>

19:39.750 --> 19:43.000
<b>What's gotten into you, Jinya-kun?</b>

19:43.710 --> 19:47.210
<b>Did something happen
with that unusual ukiyo-e painting?</b>

19:48.040 --> 19:50.420
<b>No, it wasn't a big deal.</b>

19:51.040 --> 19:51.710
<b>But...</b>

19:52.460 --> 19:56.750
<b>I ended up learning about a side of my foster father
that I never knew before.</b>

19:56.750 --> 19:58.130
<b>It was kind of startling.</b>

19:58.580 --> 20:00.210
<b>That's just how dads are.</b>

20:00.880 --> 20:04.460
<b>Mine is the same. Not everything
about him is sunshine and rainbows.</b>

20:05.080 --> 20:08.630
<b>He has a loud mouth.
Plus, he freaks out at the drop of a hat.</b>

20:08.790 --> 20:10.670
<b>And he can be a total blockhead at times.</b>

20:11.080 --> 20:13.420
<b>Hey! You're talking about me, aren'tcha?</b>

20:14.210 --> 20:15.920
<b>Perish the thought.</b>

20:15.920 --> 20:17.210
<b>Uh-huh.</b>

20:19.500 --> 20:22.210
<b>But that's all part of who my dad is.</b>

20:24.330 --> 20:25.750
<b>I guess you're right.</b>

20:29.670 --> 20:32.290
<b>There were no problems with that ukiyo-e painting.</b>

20:33.330 --> 20:37.630
<b>Its "demonic" reputation was merely the result
of the artist voicing some regrets that he had.</b>

20:38.540 --> 20:41.210
<b>No harm will come from it, whether it's kept or sold.</b>

20:41.540 --> 20:44.080
<b>What about the death it supposedly caused?</b>

20:44.420 --> 20:47.250
<b>Forgive my blunt choice of words,
but mere happenstance.</b>

20:47.830 --> 20:52.790
<b>It's true that an individual who owned the painting
passed away, but I obtained that copy for myself</b>

20:52.960 --> 20:54.750
<b>and found nothing suspect about it.</b>

20:55.250 --> 20:59.000
<b>All right. Doesn't sound like
anything to make a fuss about.</b>

20:59.460 --> 21:02.040
<b>Just strokes of good and bad luck, eh?</b>

21:02.790 --> 21:06.210
<b>Thanks for solving it. I'll fetch your pay before you leave.</b>

21:06.790 --> 21:08.920
<b>For now, let's wet the ol' whistle.</b>

21:10.880 --> 21:12.250
<b>Here, you first.</b>

21:19.040 --> 21:20.250
<b>Now it's your turn.</b>

21:29.290 --> 21:31.750
<b>Is sake something that you partake in often?</b>

21:34.040 --> 21:36.380
<b>Drinking used to only be an escape for me.</b>

21:39.830 --> 21:42.710
<b>But at some point, it became more of a pastime.</b>

21:43.540 --> 21:46.130
<b>Especially since recent brews have good flavor.</b>

21:46.960 --> 21:49.210
<b>And you? Do you have a taste for it?</b>

21:49.540 --> 21:50.130
<b>Yes.</b>

21:51.000 --> 21:53.250
<b>Enough to enjoy a cup or two at night, at least.</b>

21:57.380 --> 22:00.500
<b>Well then, we should do this again sometime.</b>

22:05.500 --> 22:08.290
<b>Certainly. It would be my pleasure.</b>
